Set-Location -LiteralPath $PSScriptRoot
$msg = 'god sales workspace: a brand with no sales team was reported as a missing membership. Entering any brand except the one seeded brand and opening its Sales Workspace said No active brand sales membership. That message was wrong twice over. sales_access.sales_org_ids does not read memberships at all in its god branch - it returns the brand sales orgs of the SELECTED brand, or all of them when the owner is neutral - so an empty result for god never meant no membership. It meant the selected brand had no BrandSalesOrg row. And nothing outside the demo seeder has ever created one: there is no other code path in the product that makes a brand sales org, so exactly one brand had a sales team, its card worked, and every other card led to a screen naming a permission problem that did not exist and could not be fixed by granting a permission. Mikes EvoSys membership was NOT what made EvoSys work, which the new gate proves by giving its god zero memberships anywhere and still entering every configured brand. Two different conditions had one message, so _no_workspace_error splits them: god with a brand selected is told that BRAND has no sales team yet and it is named from the platform record; god neutral is told no brand has one; everyone else keeps the membership refusal byte for byte. 409 rather than 403 because nothing is being refused - the workspace does not exist yet, and the fix is to create it rather than to ask for access. Adds the missing half of the doorway that Workspaces has implied since it shipped: POST god/platform/brands/{id}/sales-org, god only, audited, named and slugged from the brand itself so no brand is hardcoded, and refusing a second one with 409 rather than silently duplicating. It creates NO membership for the owner or anyone - god reaches the workspace through god authority plus the selected brand, and a membership row would be a fake employment record standing in for an authorization answer the system already has. Workspaces now reads brand_sales_orgs from the overview payload it was already being sent and ignoring: a brand with a sales team offers Enter, a brand without offers Create sales team, so no card leads to a dead end. SalesShell stops asserting a membership problem it cannot know about and renders the servers own reason. Normal enforcement is untouched and re asserted: a rep with a membership enters their own brand, a user with none is refused by require_sales_member before any context resolution, a brand header lets nobody in and does not move a rep into a brand they do not belong to, and a non god cannot create a sales team. Gate 28 covers all nine cases including no cross brand leakage after switching, A to B to A returning A B A rather than a sticky first answer, and neutral widening back to every brand.'
& "$PSScriptRoot\deploy.ps1" -Message $msg
Write-Output ("DEPLOY_EXIT=" + $LASTEXITCODE)
